        <skos:editorialNote xml:lang="fr">Terme d'oeso-phis 3.3 importé selon MIREOT (même IRI, ontologie source déclarée par rdfs:isDefinedBy) : oeso-phis n'est pas chargé avec ce module.</skos:editorialNote>
    </owl:Class>


    <!-- Axiome d'oeso-phis : tout objet scientifique peut avoir un matériel génétique (hasGermplasm, facultatif). -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.opensilex.org/vocabulary/oeso#ScientificObject">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="phisScientificObjectGermplasm"/>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="phisScientificObjectGermplasm">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.opensilex.org/vocabulary/oeso#hasGermplasm"/>
        <owl:minQualifiedCardinality rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#nonNegativeInteger">0</owl:minQualifiedCardinality>
        <owl:onClass rdf:resource="http://www.opensilex.org/vocabulary/oeso#Germplasm"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.opensilex.org/vocabulary/oeso#ScientificObject"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="phisScientificObjectGermplasm"/>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="http://www.opensilex.org/vocabulary/oeso-phis"/>
        <skos:editorialNote xml:lang="fr">Axiome d'oeso-phis 3.3, repris parce qu'oeso-phis n'est pas chargé : sans lui, les formulaires d'OpenSILEX ne proposent le matériel génétique sur aucun objet scientifique. Il devrait être déplacé dans oeso-core, qui déclare déjà hasGermplasm (domaine ScientificObject).</skos:editorialNote>
    </owl:Axiom>




    <!--
    ///////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
    //
    // Classes
    //
    ///////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
     -->


    <!-- ===== Installations agrivoltaïques ===== -->


    <!-- http://www.opensilex.org/vocabulary/oeso-agrivoltaics#AgrivoltaicInstallation -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.opensilex.org/vocabulary/oeso-agrivoltaics#AgrivoltaicInstallation">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.opensilex.org/vocabulary/oeso#ScientificObject"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="fr">installation agrivoltaïque</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">agrivoltaic installation</rdfs:label>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="fr">ombrière agrivoltaïque</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">agri-photovoltaic system</skos:altLabel>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="fr">Installation de production d'électricité utilisant l'énergie radiative du soleil et dont les modules sont situés sur une parcelle agricole où ils contribuent durablement à l'installation, au maintien ou au développement d'une production agricole.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Electricity generation installation using the radiative energy of the sun, whose modules are located on an agricultural plot where they contribute durably to establishing, maintaining or developing an agricultural production (translation of the French Energy Code, art. L314-36).</rdfs:comment>
        <dc:source>Code de l'énergie, article L314-36 (créé par la loi n° 2023-175 du 10 mars 2023, art. 54). https://www.legifrance.gouv.fr/codes/article_lc/LEGIARTI000047298015</dc:source>
        <dc:source>Décret n° 2024-318 du 8 avril 2024 relatif au développement de l'agrivoltaïsme et aux conditions d'implantation des installations photovoltaïques sur des terrains agricoles, naturels ou forestiers. https://www.legifrance.gouv.fr/eli/decret/2024/4/8/ECOR2321918D/jo/texte</dc:source>
        <dc:source>DIN SPEC 91434:2021-05. Agri-photovoltaic systems - Requirements for primary agricultural use. https://www.dinmedia.de/de/technische-regel/din-spec-91434/337886742</dc:source>
        <dc:source>Dupraz C., Marrou H., Talbot G., Dufour L., Nogier A., Ferard Y. (2011). Combining solar photovoltaic panels and food crops for optimising land use: Towards new agrivoltaic schemes. Renewable Energy 36(10):2725-2732. https://doi.org/10.1016/j.renene.2011.03.005</dc:source>
        <dc:source>AGROVOC c_9e7141ec agrivoltaic systems. http://aims.fao.org/aos/agrovoc/c_9e7141ec</dc:source>
        <skos:relatedMatch rdf:resource="http://aims.fao.org/aos/agrovoc/c_9e7141ec"/>
        <dcterms:replaces rdf:resource="http://www.opensilex.org/vocabulary/oeso#ShadeHouse"/>
    </owl:Class>


    <!-- http://www.opensilex.org/vocabulary/oeso-agrivoltaics#SolarPanel -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.opensilex.org/vocabulary/oeso-agrivoltaics#SolarPanel">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.opensilex.org/vocabulary/oeso#ScientificObject"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="fr">panneau solaire</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">solar panel</rdfs:label>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="fr">panneau photovoltaïque</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">photovoltaic panel</skos:altLabel>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="fr">Panneau composé d'un ou de plusieurs modules photovoltaïques qui convertissent le rayonnement solaire en électricité. (non sourcé)</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Panel made of one or several photovoltaic modules that convert solar radiation into electricity. (not sourced)</rdfs:comment>
        <skos:closeMatch rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/seas/SolarPanel"/>
        <dcterms:replaces rdf:resource="http://www.opensilex.org/vocabulary/oeso#Panel"/>
        <dcterms:replaces rdf:resource="http://www.opensilex.org/vocabulary/oeso#SolarPanel"/>
        <skos:editorialNote xml:lang="fr">La classe seas:SolarPanel existe mais n'a pas de définition : la définition reste à sourcer.</skos:editorialNote>
    </owl:Class>


    <!-- ===== Parcellaire ===== -->


    <!-- http://www.opensilex.org/vocabulary/oeso-agrivoltaics#SubPlot -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.opensilex.org/vocabulary/oeso-agrivoltaics#SubPlot">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.opensilex.org/vocabulary/oeso-vitis#PlotComponent"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="fr">sous-parcelle</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">subplot</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="fr">Subdivision d'une placette expérimentale (oeso-vitis:ExperimentalPlot), par exemple pour distinguer des variétés. (non sourcé)</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Subdivision of an experimental plot (oeso-vitis:ExperimentalPlot), for example to distinguish varieties. (not sourced)</rdfs:comment>
        <dcterms:replaces rdf:resource="http://www.opensilex.org/vocabulary/oeso#SubPlot"/>
    </owl:Class>


    <!-- ===== Structures végétales ===== -->


    <!-- http://www.opensilex.org/vocabulary/oeso-agrivoltaics#Fruit -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.opensilex.org/vocabulary/oeso-agrivoltaics#Fruit">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.opensilex.org/vocabulary/oeso-vitis#PlantOrgan"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="fr">fruit</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">fruit</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="fr">Structure végétale multi-tissulaire (PO:0025496) qui se développe à partir d'un gynécée (PO:0009062) ou d'un carpelle unique (PO:0009030) et qui, à maturité, peut contenir une ou plusieurs graines (PO:0009010).</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A multi-tissue plant structure (PO:0025496) that develops from a gynoecium (PO:0009062), or a single carpel (PO:0009030), and at maturity may have as parts one or more seeds (PO:0009010).</rdfs:comment>
        <dc:source>Plant Ontology, PO:0009001 fruit. http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PO_0009001</dc:source>
        <skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PO_0009001"/>
        <skos:narrowMatch rdf:resource="http://www.opensilex.org/vocabulary/oeso-vitis#Berry"/>
        <dcterms:replaces rdf:resource="http://www.opensilex.org/vocabulary/oeso#Fruit"/>
    </owl:Class>


    <!-- http://www.opensilex.org/vocabulary/oeso-agrivoltaics#Apple -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.opensilex.org/vocabulary/oeso-agrivoltaics#Apple">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.opensilex.org/vocabulary/oeso-agrivoltaics#Fruit"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="fr">pomme</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">apple</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="fr">Fruit de type pomme (PO:0030110) du pommier (Malus domestica, AGROVOC c_4555).</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Pome fruit (PO:0030110) of the apple tree (Malus domestica, AGROVOC c_4555).</rdfs:comment>
        <dc:source>AGROVOC c_541 apples. http://aims.fao.org/aos/agrovoc/c_541</dc:source>
        <dc:source>Plant Ontology, PO:0030110 pome fruit. http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PO_0030110</dc:source>
        <skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://aims.fao.org/aos/agrovoc/c_541"/>
        <skos:broadMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PO_0030110"/>
        <dcterms:replaces rdf:resource="http://www.opensilex.org/vocabulary/oeso#Apple"/>
    </owl:Class>


    <!-- http://www.opensilex.org/vocabulary/oeso-agrivoltaics#Tomato -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.opensilex.org/vocabulary/oeso-agrivoltaics#Tomato">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.opensilex.org/vocabulary/oeso-agrivoltaics#Fruit"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="fr">tomate</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">tomato</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="fr">Fruit de type baie (PO:0030108) du plant de tomate (Solanum lycopersicum, AGROVOC c_4475).</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Berry fruit (PO:0030108) of the tomato plant (Solanum lycopersicum, AGROVOC c_4475).</rdfs:comment>
        <dc:source>AGROVOC c_7805 tomatoes. http://aims.fao.org/aos/agrovoc/c_7805</dc:source>
        <dc:source>Plant Ontology, PO:0030108 berry fruit. http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PO_0030108</dc:source>
        <skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://aims.fao.org/aos/agrovoc/c_7805"/>
        <skos:broadMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PO_0030108"/>
        <dcterms:replaces rdf:resource="http://www.opensilex.org/vocabulary/oeso#Tomato"/>
    </owl:Class>


    <!-- http://www.opensilex.org/vocabulary/oeso-agrivoltaics#Corymb -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.opensilex.org/vocabulary/oeso-agrivoltaics#Corymb">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.opensilex.org/vocabulary/oeso-vitis#Inflorescence"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="fr">corymbe</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">corymb</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="fr">Inflorescence (PO:0009049) à croissance à la fois monopodiale et sympodiale qui, au stade floraison (PO:0007616), se compose d'un axe d'inflorescence de premier ordre déterminé (PO:0025104) et d'axes d'ordre supérieur déterminés (PO:0020122) portant des fleurs pédicellées (PO:0009046) qui forment ensemble un plan de fleurs convexe.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An inflorescence (PO:0009049) with both monopodial and sympodial growth habits, which at flowering stage (PO:0007616), is composed of a determinate, first order inflorescence axis (PO:0025104), and determinate higher order inflorescence axes (PO:0020122) with pedicellate flowers (PO:0009046) that collectively form a convex plane of flowers.</rdfs:comment>
        <dc:source>Plant Ontology, PO:0030124 corymb inflorescence. http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PO_0030124</dc:source>
        <skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PO_0030124"/>
        <dcterms:replaces rdf:resource="http://www.opensilex.org/vocabulary/oeso#Corymbe"/>
    </owl:Class>


    <!-- http://www.opensilex.org/vocabulary/oeso-agrivoltaics#Truss -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.opensilex.org/vocabulary/oeso-agrivoltaics#Truss">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.opensilex.org/vocabulary/oeso-vitis#Inflorescence"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="fr">bouquet</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">truss</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="fr">Inflorescence (PO:0009049) du plant de tomate (Solanum lycopersicum).</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Inflorescence (PO:0009049) of the tomato plant (Solanum lycopersicum), referred to as a truss in tomato.</rdfs:comment>
        <dc:source>Silva Ferreira D., Kevei Z., Kurowski T., de Noronha Fonseca M.E., Mohareb F., Boiteux L.S., Thompson A.J. (2018). BIFURCATE FLOWER TRUSS: a novel locus controlling inflorescence branching in tomato contains a defective MAP kinase gene. Journal of Experimental Botany 69(10):2581-2593. https://doi.org/10.1093/jxb/ery076</dc:source>
        <skos:broadMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PO_0009049"/>
        <dcterms:replaces rdf:resource="http://www.opensilex.org/vocabulary/oeso#Truss"/>
    </owl:Class>


    <!-- http://www.opensilex.org/vocabulary/oeso-agrivoltaics#Branch -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.opensilex.org/vocabulary/oeso-agrivoltaics#Branch">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.opensilex.org/vocabulary/oeso-vitis#PlantOrgan"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="fr">branche</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">branch</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="fr">Axe de pousse (PO:0025029) qui se développe à partir d'un méristème de bourgeon axillaire (PO:0000232) ou de divisions égales d'une cellule apicale méristématique (PO:0030007).</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A shoot axis (PO:0025029) that develops from an axillary bud meristem (PO:0000232) or from equal divisions of a meristematic apical cell (PO:0030007).</rdfs:comment>
        <dc:source>Plant Ontology, PO:0025073 branch. http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PO_0025073</dc:source>
        <dc:source>AGROVOC c_23995 branches. http://aims.fao.org/aos/agrovoc/c_23995</dc:source>
        <skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PO_0025073"/>
        <skos:closeMatch rdf:resource="http://aims.fao.org/aos/agrovoc/c_23995"/>
        <dcterms:replaces rdf:resource="http://www.opensilex.org/vocabulary/oeso#Branch"/>
    </owl:Class>


    <!-- http://www.opensilex.org/vocabulary/oeso-agrivoltaics#Trunk -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.opensilex.org/vocabulary/oeso-agrivoltaics#Trunk">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.opensilex.org/vocabulary/oeso-vitis#PlantOrgan"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="fr">tronc de plante ligneuse</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">woody plant trunk</rdfs:label>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="fr">tronc</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">trunk</skos:altLabel>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="fr">Tige (PO:0009047), c'est-à-dire axe principal de la plante, d'une plante ligneuse pérenne comme un arbre ou une vigne. « Tronc » est un synonyme restreint de « tige » dans la Plant Ontology.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Stem (PO:0009047), i.e. primary axis of the plant, of a woody perennial plant such as a tree or a grapevine. 'Trunk' is a narrow synonym of 'stem' in the Plant Ontology.</rdfs:comment>
        <dc:source>Plant Ontology, PO:0009047 stem (narrow synonym: trunk). http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PO_0009047</dc:source>
        <dc:source>AGROVOC c_15017 trunks. http://aims.fao.org/aos/agrovoc/c_15017</dc:source>
        <skos:broadMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PO_0009047"/>
        <skos:closeMatch rdf:resource="http://aims.fao.org/aos/agrovoc/c_15017"/>
        <skos:narrowMatch rdf:resource="http://www.opensilex.org/vocabulary/oeso-vitis#Trunk"/>
        <dcterms:replaces rdf:resource="http://www.opensilex.org/vocabulary/oeso#Trunc"/>
    </owl:Class>


    <!-- http://www.opensilex.org/vocabulary/oeso-agrivoltaics#LateralShoot -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.opensilex.org/vocabulary/oeso-agrivoltaics#LateralShoot">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.opensilex.org/vocabulary/oeso-vitis#Shoot"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="fr">rameau latéral</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">lateral shoot</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="fr">Rameau qui se développe à partir d'un bourgeon axillaire (PO:0004709) ; correspond au système de pousse axillaire (PO:0006343) de la Plant Ontology.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Shoot that develops from an axillary bud (PO:0004709); corresponds to the axillary shoot system (PO:0006343) of the Plant Ontology.</rdfs:comment>
        <dc:source>Plant Ontology, PO:0006343 axillary shoot system. http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PO_0006343</dc:source>
        <skos:closeMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PO_0006343"/>
        <dcterms:replaces rdf:resource="http://www.opensilex.org/vocabulary/oeso#LateralShoot"/>
    </owl:Class>


    <!-- http://www.opensilex.org/vocabulary/oeso-agrivoltaics#TerminalShoot -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.opensilex.org/vocabulary/oeso-agrivoltaics#TerminalShoot">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.opensilex.org/vocabulary/oeso-vitis#Shoot"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="fr">rameau terminal</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">terminal shoot</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="fr">Rameau issu du bourgeon terminal (apical) d'un axe. (non sourcé)</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Shoot that develops from the terminal (apical) bud of an axis. (not sourced)</rdfs:comment>
        <dcterms:replaces rdf:resource="http://www.opensilex.org/vocabulary/oeso#TerminalShoot"/>
    </owl:Class>


    <!-- http://www.opensilex.org/vocabulary/oeso-agrivoltaics#BourseShoot -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.opensilex.org/vocabulary/oeso-agrivoltaics#BourseShoot">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.opensilex.org/vocabulary/oeso-vitis#Shoot"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="fr">pousse de bourse</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">bourse shoot</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="fr">Pousse végétative qui se développe à partir d'un bourgeon axillaire de la bourse, axe court et renflé issu du bourgeon floral du pommier.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Vegetative shoot that develops from an axillary bud on the bourse, the short swollen axis into which the floral bud of the apple tree develops.</rdfs:comment>
        <dc:source>Wang Y.-T., Pallas B., Salazar-Gutierrez M.R., Costes E., Hoogenboom G. (2020). A comparative study on the branching pattern of monocyclic and bicyclic shoots of apple cv. 'Fuji'. Frontiers in Plant Science 11:571918. https://doi.org/10.3389/fpls.2020.571918</dc:source>
        <dc:source>Pratt C. (1988). Apple flower and fruit: morphology and anatomy. Horticultural Reviews, pp. 273-308. https://doi.org/10.1002/9781118060834.ch8</dc:source>
        <dcterms:replaces rdf:resource="http://www.opensilex.org/vocabulary/oeso#bourseShoot"/>
    </owl:Class>


    <!-- http://www.opensilex.org/vocabulary/oeso-agrivoltaics#EpicormicShoot -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.opensilex.org/vocabulary/oeso-agrivoltaics#EpicormicShoot">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.opensilex.org/vocabulary/oeso-vitis#Shoot"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="fr">gourmand</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">epicormic shoot</rdfs:label>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">water sprout</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">stem sucker</skos:altLabel>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="fr">Pousse qui se développe à partir d'une tige (PO:0009047), par exemple sur le tronc ou sur une branche (PO:0004546 epicormic shoot system).</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Shoot system developing from a stem (PO:0009047), for example on the trunk or on a branch (PO:0004546 epicormic shoot system).</rdfs:comment>
        <dc:source>Plant Ontology, PO:0004546 epicormic shoot system (exact synonym: stem sucker). http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PO_0004546</dc:source>
        <skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PO_0004546"/>
        <dcterms:replaces rdf:resource="http://www.opensilex.org/vocabulary/oeso#Sucker"/>
        <dcterms:replaces rdf:resource="http://www.opensilex.org/vocabulary/oeso#waterSprout"/>
        <skos:editorialNote xml:lang="fr">Fusion de oeso:waterSprout (gourmand du pommier) et oeso:Sucker (gourmand de la vigne) : l'espèce est portée par le matériel génétique, pas par le type d'organe (OOPS! P02). À valider.</skos:editorialNote>
    </owl:Class>


    <!-- http://www.opensilex.org/vocabulary/oeso-agrivoltaics#Terminal -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.opensilex.org/vocabulary/oeso-agrivoltaics#Terminal">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.opensilex.org/vocabulary/oeso#ScientificObject"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="fr">terminal</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">terminal</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="fr">Concept repris de oeso-sunagri, où il n'avait pas de définition ; son sens doit être précisé par un expert du domaine. (non sourcé)</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Concept taken over from oeso-sunagri, where it had no definition; its meaning must be specified by a domain expert. (not sourced)</rdfs:comment>
        <dcterms:replaces rdf:resource="http://www.opensilex.org/vocabulary/oeso#Terminal"/>
        <skos:editorialNote xml:lang="fr">Sens inconnu : à définir ou à déprécier.</skos:editorialNote>
    </owl:Class>


    <!-- ===== Capteurs ===== -->


    <!-- http://www.opensilex.org/vocabulary/oeso-agrivoltaics#Dendrometer -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.opensilex.org/vocabulary/oeso-agrivoltaics#Dendrometer">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.opensilex.org/vocabulary/oeso#SensingDevice"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="fr">dendromètre</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">dendrometer</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="fr">Appareil de mesure des faibles variations du diamètre d'un tronc d'arbre, comme les contractions et les gonflements qui accompagnent les fluctuations journalières de la transpiration.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Device for measuring small changes in the diameter of a tree trunk, such as the minute amounts of shrinkage and swelling that accompany the daily fluctuations in transpiration.</rdfs:comment>
        <dc:source>EnvThes 20365 dendrometer (definition from Henderson's Dictionary of Biology). http://vocabs.lter-europe.net/EnvThes/20365</dc:source>
        <dc:source>Drew D.M., Downes G.M. (2009). The use of precision dendrometers in research on daily stem size and wood property variation: A review. Dendrochronologia 27(2):159-172. https://doi.org/10.1016/j.dendro.2009.06.008</dc:source>
        <skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://vocabs.lter-europe.net/EnvThes/20365"/>
        <skos:closeMatch rdf:resource="https://lod.nal.usda.gov/nalt/32311"/>
        <dcterms:replaces rdf:resource="http://www.opensilex.org/vocabulary/oeso#Dendrometer"/>
        <skos:editorialNote xml:lang="fr">Concept générique, candidat pour oeso-core.</skos:editorialNote>
    </owl:Class>


    <!-- ===== Organisations ===== -->


    <!-- http://www.opensilex.org/vocabulary/oeso-agrivoltaics#LocalInfrastructure -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.opensilex.org/vocabulary/oeso-agrivoltaics#LocalInfrastructure">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/Organization"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="fr">infrastructure locale</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">local infrastructure</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="fr">Groupe d'installations situées sur un même site et dépendant d'une ou de plusieurs institutions, qui partagent des comités de gouvernance, un système d'information commun (ou du moins très interopérable), des principes communs de calcul des coûts et de tarification, et un outil commun d'accès des utilisateurs. (non sourcé)</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Group of installations located in one site depending on one institution (or more), which share governance committees, a common (or at least highly interoperable) information system, common principles for cost calculation and pricing and a common tool for user access. (not sourced)</rdfs:comment>
        <dcterms:replaces rdf:resource="http://www.opensilex.org/vocabulary/oeso#LocalInfrastructure"/>
        <skos:editorialNote xml:lang="fr">Concept générique, candidat pour oeso-core.</skos:editorialNote>
    </owl:Class>


    <!-- http://www.opensilex.org/vocabulary/oeso-agrivoltaics#NationalInfrastructure -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.opensilex.org/vocabulary/oeso-agrivoltaics#NationalInfrastructure">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/Organization"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="fr">infrastructure nationale</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">national infrastructure</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="fr">Groupe organisé d'infrastructures locales dont la gouvernance est reconnue par les autorités nationales (ministère ou structures nationales). (non sourcé)</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Organised group of local infrastructures with governance recognised by national authorities (e.g. the relevant ministry or national structures). (not sourced)</rdfs:comment>
        <dcterms:replaces rdf:resource="http://www.opensilex.org/vocabulary/oeso#NationalInfrastructure"/>
        <skos:editorialNote xml:lang="fr">Concept générique, candidat pour oeso-core.</skos:editorialNote>
    </owl:Class>


    <!-- http://www.opensilex.org/vocabulary/oeso-agrivoltaics#EuropeanInfrastructure -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.opensilex.org/vocabulary/oeso-agrivoltaics#EuropeanInfrastructure">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/Organization"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="fr">infrastructure européenne</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">european infrastructure</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="fr">Infrastructure de recherche organisée à l'échelle européenne, qui regroupe des infrastructures nationales, par exemple le projet ESFRI EMPHASIS (https://emphasis.plant-phenotyping.eu/). (non sourcé)</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Research infrastructure organised at European level that groups national infrastructures, for example the ESFRI project EMPHASIS (https://emphasis.plant-phenotyping.eu/). (not sourced)</rdfs:comment>
        <dcterms:replaces rdf:resource="http://www.opensilex.org/vocabulary/oeso#EuropeanInfrastructure"/>
        <skos:editorialNote xml:lang="fr">L'ancien commentaire décrivait le projet EMPHASIS au lieu de définir le concept.</skos:editorialNote>
    </owl:Class>


    <!-- http://www.opensilex.org/vocabulary/oeso-agrivoltaics#Platform -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.opensilex.org/vocabulary/oeso-agrivoltaics#Platform">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/Organization"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="fr">plateforme</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">platform</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="fr">Organisation qui met à disposition des équipements et des compétences partagés pour des expérimentations, par exemple une plateforme de phénotypage. (non sourcé)</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Organisation that provides shared equipment and expertise for experiments, for example a phenotyping platform. (not sourced)</rdfs:comment>
        <dcterms:replaces rdf:resource="http://www.opensilex.org/vocabulary/oeso#Platform"/>
        <skos:editorialNote xml:lang="fr">L'ancien concept n'avait aucune super-classe et n'apparaissait donc pas dans OpenSILEX.</skos:editorialNote>
    </owl:Class>


    <!-- http://www.opensilex.org/vocabulary/oeso-agrivoltaics#ExperimentalSite -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.opensilex.org/vocabulary/oeso-agrivoltaics#ExperimentalSite">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.opensilex.org/vocabulary/oeso#ExperimentalUnit"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="fr">site expérimental</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">experimental site</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="fr">Site où sont conduites des expérimentations, rattaché à une unité expérimentale. (non sourcé)</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Site where experiments are carried out, attached to an experimental unit. (not sourced)</rdfs:comment>
        <dcterms:replaces rdf:resource="http://www.opensilex.org/vocabulary/oeso#ExperimentalSite"/>
    </owl:Class>


    <!-- ===== Documents ===== -->


    <!-- http://www.opensilex.org/vocabulary/oeso-agrivoltaics#ExperimentalDesign -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.opensilex.org/vocabulary/oeso-agrivoltaics#ExperimentalDesign">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.opensilex.org/vocabulary/oeso#ScientificDocument"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="fr">plan d'expérience</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">experimental design</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="fr">Document qui décrit le plan d'une expérimentation, c'est-à-dire la spécification des protocoles exécutés dans le cadre d'une investigation (OBI:0500000 study design).</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Document describing the design of an experiment, i.e. the plan specification comprising the protocols executed as part of an investigation (OBI:0500000 study design).</rdfs:comment>
        <dc:source>Ontology for Biomedical Investigations, OBI:0500000 study design. http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0500000</dc:source>
        <skos:closeMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0500000"/>
        <dcterms:replaces rdf:resource="http://www.opensilex.org/vocabulary/oeso#ExperimentalDesign"/>
    </owl:Class>


    <!-- http://www.opensilex.org/vocabulary/oeso-agrivoltaics#MasterThesis -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.opensilex.org/vocabulary/oeso-agrivoltaics#MasterThesis">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.opensilex.org/vocabulary/oeso#ScientificDocument"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="fr">mémoire de master</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">master's thesis</rdfs:label>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="fr">rapport de stage de master</skos:altLabel>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="fr">Mémoire rédigé pour l'obtention d'un diplôme de master (concept aligné sur fabio:MastersThesis).</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Thesis written for a master's degree (aligned with fabio:MastersThesis).</rdfs:comment>
        <dc:source>Peroni S., Shotton D. (2012). FaBiO and CiTO: ontologies for describing bibliographic resources and citations. Journal of Web Semantics 17:33-43. http://purl.org/spar/fabio/</dc:source>
        <skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.org/spar/fabio/MastersThesis"/>
        <dcterms:replaces rdf:resource="http://www.opensilex.org/vocabulary/oeso#MasterThesis"/>
    </owl:Class>


    <!-- http://www.opensilex.org/vocabulary/oeso-agrivoltaics#PhDThesis -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.opensilex.org/vocabulary/oeso-agrivoltaics#PhDThesis">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.opensilex.org/vocabulary/oeso#ScientificDocument"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="fr">thèse de doctorat</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">doctoral thesis</rdfs:label>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">PhD thesis</skos:altLabel>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="fr">Thèse rédigée pour l'obtention d'un doctorat (concept aligné sur fabio:DoctoralThesis).</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Thesis written for a doctoral degree (aligned with fabio:DoctoralThesis).</rdfs:comment>
        <dc:source>Peroni S., Shotton D. (2012). FaBiO and CiTO: ontologies for describing bibliographic resources and citations. Journal of Web Semantics 17:33-43. http://purl.org/spar/fabio/</dc:source>
        <skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://purl.org/spar/fabio/DoctoralThesis"/>
        <dcterms:replaces rdf:resource="http://www.opensilex.org/vocabulary/oeso#PhDThesis"/>
    </owl:Class>


    <!-- ===== Événements ===== -->


    <!-- http://www.opensilex.org/vocabulary/oeso-agrivoltaics#ManualThinning -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.opensilex.org/vocabulary/oeso-agrivoltaics#ManualThinning">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.opensilex.org/vocabulary/oeev#Thinning"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="fr">éclaircissage manuel</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">manual thinning</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="fr">Éclaircissage des fruits (AGROVOC c_32701) réalisé à la main, en supprimant des fleurs à la fin du printemps ou des jeunes fruits après la nouaison.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Fruit thinning (AGROVOC c_32701) carried out by hand, by removing flowers in late spring or fruitlets after fruit set.</rdfs:comment>
        <dc:source>AGROVOC c_32701 defruiting (alternative label: fruit thinning). http://aims.fao.org/aos/agrovoc/c_32701</dc:source>
        <dc:source>Costa G., Botton A., Vizzotto G. (2018). Fruit thinning: advances and trends. Horticultural Reviews 46:185-226. https://doi.org/10.1002/9781119521082.ch4</dc:source>
        <skos:broadMatch rdf:resource="http://aims.fao.org/aos/agrovoc/c_32701"/>
        <dcterms:replaces rdf:resource="http://www.opensilex.org/vocabulary/oeev#ManualThinning"/>
    </owl:Class>


    <!-- http://www.opensilex.org/vocabulary/oeso-agrivoltaics#Drought -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://www.opensilex.org/vocabulary/oeso-agrivoltaics#Drought">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.opensilex.org/vocabulary/oeev#Incident"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="fr">sécheresse</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">drought</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="fr">Période exceptionnelle de manque d'eau pour les écosystèmes et la population (due à de faibles précipitations, à une température élevée et/ou au vent) (traduction du glossaire du GIEC).</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An exceptional period of water shortage for existing ecosystems and the human population (due to low rainfall, high temperature, and/or wind).</rdfs:comment>
        <dc:source>IPCC (2021). Annex VII: Glossary [Matthews J.B.R. et al. (eds.)]. In: Climate Change 2021: The Physical Science Basis. Cambridge University Press, pp. 2215-2256. https://doi.org/10.1017/9781009157896.022</dc:source>
        <dc:source>AGROVOC c_2391 drought. http://aims.fao.org/aos/agrovoc/c_2391</dc:source>
        <skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://aims.fao.org/aos/agrovoc/c_2391"/>
        <dcterms:replaces rdf:resource="http://www.opensilex.org/vocabulary/oeev#Drought"/>
    </owl:Class>




